{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments ["<b>That place he called Naḥal Eshkol.</b> For from many days earlier this place had already been called \"Eshkol,\" as is derived in the Yalkut, parashat Ḥayei Sarah (102:23) and in this parashah (743:13), and by means of this event they called it \"Naḥal Eshkol\" — they added to it the name \"Naḥal,\" and this is to the praise of the land of Israel, for the principal fine vine is that which grows in the mountains, for they ripen more by means of the sun, which holds greater sway in the mountains than in the valleys, and they took the cluster from the naḥal in the valley, and even so it was large and superior — and all the more so the clusters of the mountains. And by this the question is resolved, why they did not call it simply \"Eshkol.\"\n\nAnd above, in parashat Naso (5:17), in the matter of the bitter waters, I explained that the waters of Marah were sweet, and in the mouths of Israel they reverted to being bitter; therefore it was necessary to say there, \"עַל כֵּן קָרָא שְׁמָהּ מָרָה\" — lest it be understood from the name Marah that they were bitter beforehand.\n\nSo too in the Akedah he explained that it was necessary to inform us that it was called \"Eshkol\" on account of this cluster that they cut from there — lest you say that it had always been called Eshkol because there are choice clusters there, which would be testimony to the dispraise of the land, that in all the land there is nothing like them. Therefore he said that in all the land it was so, and they took by chance from whatever came to hand, and what was called \"Naḥal Eshkol\" is on account of the cluster.\n\nAnd it is possible to explain that it was called Eshkol on account of \"לָמָּה אֶשְׁכַּל שְׁנֵיכֶם יוֹם אֶחָד\" — for this place caused them to become bereaved, for they said: just as its fruit is abnormal, so is its people, and by means of this the children of Israel were cut off from there, for all of them were cut off, perished and ended. Therefore it says, \"אֲשֶׁר כָּרְתוּ מִשָּׁם בְּנֵי יִשְׂרָאֵל.\""], :book :numbers, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 13, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:41:11.267539343Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}